Deployment
==========
Live at https://xiaobinmei.com (GitHub Pages, gh-pages branch).

Custom domain setup (already done — recorded for reference):
* public/CNAME contains "xiaobinmei.com". It MUST live in public/, not just in
  GitHub's Settings UI: `gh-pages -d dist` removes files absent from dist on
  every deploy, so a CNAME written by the UI gets wiped. Vite copies public/*
  into dist/ verbatim.
* vite.config.js uses base: '/'. A custom domain serves from the root, so the
  old '/XiaobinMei/' subpath would 404 every asset and render a blank page.
* DNS at the registrar:
    apex  xiaobinmei.com   A     185.199.108.153
                                 185.199.109.153
                                 185.199.110.153
                                 185.199.111.153
                           AAAA  2606:50c0:8000::153
                                 2606:50c0:8001::153
                                 2606:50c0:8002::153
                                 2606:50c0:8003::153
    www                    CNAME jadeni77.github.io
* GitHub: Settings -> Pages -> Custom domain = xiaobinmei.com, Enforce HTTPS on.

To deploy
=========
* npm run deploy      (runs the build first via predeploy)

Local dev
=========
* npm run dev         -> http://localhost:5173/   (root now, not /XiaobinMei/)
* npm test            -> vitest
* npm run lint


Previous:
To Deploy:
* Add "homepage": "https://jadeni77.github.io/XiaobinMei" (or "homepage": "link") in package.json.
* Add base: '/XiaobinMei/' or (base: '/repo name/') to vite.config.js.
* Add "deploy": "gh-pages -d dist" to package.json in 'script'.
* Make sure "npm install gh-pages --save-dev" in install

To Edit:
* Edit as usual
* npm run build to save changes
* npm run deploy to push contents to the gh-pages branch
* Visit website